360e042f-0b16-42fc-9b9a-116761c6c27f	\N	cfe93849-b68e-4d70-8177-028bf69cdc6a	Heater Cartridge and NTC Thermsitor for Kobra 2 Series	heater-cartridge-and-ntc-thermsitor-for-kobra-2-series	heater-cartridge-and-ntc-thermsitor-for-kobra-2-series	<h3 data-start="218" data-end="298"><strong data-start="222" data-end="298">Heater Cartridge and NTC Thermistor Set (Compatible with Kobra 2 Series)</strong></h3>\n<p data-start="300" data-end="646">This heater cartridge and NTC thermistor set is a high-quality replacement component designed for stable and accurate temperature control in 3D printer hotend systems. Built for durability and precision, it ensures efficient heating performance and reliable temperature sensing, making it ideal for consistent extrusion and high-quality prints.</p>\n<p data-start="648" data-end="667"><strong data-start="648" data-end="665">Key Features:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="668" data-end="1292">\n<li data-start="668" data-end="775">\n<p data-start="670" data-end="775"><strong data-start="670" data-end="688">Compatibility:</strong> Designed for Kobra 2 Series 3D printers (including Neo, Pro, Plus, and Max variants)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="776" data-end="796">\n<p data-start="778" data-end="796"><strong data-start="778" data-end="790">Voltage:</strong> 24V</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="797" data-end="815">\n<p data-start="799" data-end="815"><strong data-start="799" data-end="809">Power:</strong> 60W</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="816" data-end="914">\n<p data-start="818" data-end="914"><strong data-start="818" data-end="848">Heater Cartridge Material:</strong> Stainless steel element with fiberglass and silicone insulation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="915" data-end="1007">\n<p data-start="917" data-end="1007"><strong data-start="917" data-end="937">Thermistor Type:</strong> 100K NTC (3950) precision sensor for accurate temperature detection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1008" data-end="1092">\n<p data-start="1010" data-end="1092"><strong data-start="1010" data-end="1029">Connector Type:</strong> Pre-crimped plug connector for quick and secure installation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1093" data-end="1164">\n<p data-start="1095" data-end="1164"><strong data-start="1095" data-end="1116">Cable Insulation:</strong> High-temperature PTFE and fiberglass sleeving</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1165" data-end="1203">\n<p data-start="1167" data-end="1203"><strong data-start="1167" data-end="1189">Temperature Range:</strong> Up to 300°C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1204" data-end="1292">\n<p data-start="1206" data-end="1292"><strong data-start="1206" data-end="1219">Function:</strong> Provides rapid and uniform heating along with precise thermal feedback</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="1294" data-end="1311"><strong data-start="1294" data-end="1309">Advantages:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1312" data-end="1611">\n<li data-start="1312" data-end="1367">\n<p data-start="1314" data-end="1367">Consistent temperature control for stable extrusion</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1368" data-end="1420">\n<p data-start="1370" data-end="1420">Fast heat-up time with efficient energy transfer</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1421" data-end="1482">\n<p data-start="1423" data-end="1482">Durable, long-lasting materials for extended service life</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1483" data-end="1547">\n<p data-start="1485" data-end="1547">Easy plug-and-play replacement for the Kobra 2 hotend system</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1548" data-end="1611">\n<p data-start="1550" data-end="1611">Ideal for maintenance, part replacement, or hotend upgrades</p>\n</li>\n</ul>	<h3 data-start="218" data-end="298"><strong data-start="222" data-end="298">Heater Cartridge and NTC Thermistor Set (Compatible with Kobra 2 Series)</strong></h3>\n<p data-start="300" data-end="646">This heater cartridge and NTC thermistor set is a high-quality replacement component designed for stable and accurate temperature control in 3D printer hotend systems. Built for durability and precision, it ensures efficient heating performance and reliable temperature sensing, making it ideal for consistent extrusion and high-quality prints.</p>\n<p data-start="648" data-end="667"><strong data-start="648" data-end="665">Key Features:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="668" data-end="1292">\n<li data-start="668" data-end="775">\n<p data-start="670" data-end="775"><strong data-start="670" data-end="688">Compatibility:</strong> Designed for Kobra 2 Series 3D printers (including Neo, Pro, Plus, and Max variants)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="776" data-end="796">\n<p data-start="778" data-end="796"><strong data-start="778" data-end="790">Voltage:</strong> 24V</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="797" data-end="815">\n<p data-start="799" data-end="815"><strong data-start="799" data-end="809">Power:</strong> 60W</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="816" data-end="914">\n<p data-start="818" data-end="914"><strong data-start="818" data-end="848">Heater Cartridge Material:</strong> Stainless steel element with fiberglass and silicone insulation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="915" data-end="1007">\n<p data-start="917" data-end="1007"><strong data-start="917" data-end="937">Thermistor Type:</strong> 100K NTC (3950) precision sensor for accurate temperature detection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1008" data-end="1092">\n<p data-start="1010" data-end="1092"><strong data-start="1010" data-end="1029">Connector Type:</strong> Pre-crimped plug connector for quick and secure installation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1093" data-end="1164">\n<p data-start="1095" data-end="1164"><strong data-start="1095" data-end="1116">Cable Insulation:</strong> High-temperature PTFE and fiberglass sleeving</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1165" data-end="1203">\n<p data-start="1167" data-end="1203"><strong data-start="1167" data-end="1189">Temperature Range:</strong> Up to 300°C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1204" data-end="1292">\n<p data-start="1206" data-end="1292"><strong data-start="1206" data-end="1219">Function:</strong> Provides rapid and uniform heating along with precise thermal feedback</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="1294" data-end="1311"><strong data-start="1294" data-end="1309">Advantages:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1312" data-end="1611">\n<li data-start="1312" data-end="1367">\n<p data-start="1314" data-end="1367">Consistent temperature control for stable extrusion</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1368" data-end="1420">\n<p data-start="1370" data-end="1420">Fast heat-up time with efficient energy transfer</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1421" data-end="1482">\n<p data-start="1423" data-end="1482">Durable, long-lasting materials for extended service life</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1483" data-end="1547">\n<p data-start="1485" data-end="1547">Easy plug-and-play replacement for the Kobra 2 hotend system</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1548" data-end="1611">\n<p data-start="1550" data-end="1611">Ideal for maintenance, part replacement, or hotend upgrades</p>\n</li>\n</ul>	300.00	\N	\N	1	t	f	f	t	0.00	3	t	[]	[]	["https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443932483-205180634.jpg", "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443932440-742333080.jpg"]	[]	[]	[]	[]	{"title": null, "description": null}	{}	{}	[]	[]	[{"name": "Color", "value": "silver; geometric"}]	[{"name": "Type", "values": ["Heater", "Thermistor"]}]	\N	2026-07-19 06:57:04.001+00	2026-08-25 06:09:28.060538+00	0.00	g
3467913d-af27-47c1-99ed-cefa716926a0	\N	818c760a-e5d6-42fa-a68d-78bf45f3659d	Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo 3D Printer	anycubic-kobra-3-v2-combo-3d-printer	anycubic-kobra-3-v2-combo-3d-printer	<h2 data-start="243" data-end="254">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="256" data-end="645">The Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo is a high-speed, multi-colour capable FDM printer with a large build volume, designed for users wanting quicker prints, colour/multi-material options, and a lot of smart features. The “Combo” refers to the fact that it includes the <strong data-start="516" data-end="527">ACE Pro</strong> module(s) that allow multi-colour/multi-filament printing (4-color, up to 8-color if two ACE Pros are used + the hub).<br></p>\n<h2 data-start="197" data-end="231">Product Description</h2>\n<p data-start="233" data-end="450">A high-performance, feature-rich FDM 3D printer designed for speed, multi-colour capability, and versatile material use. Built for serious prototyping, creative design, and flexible, high throughput printing workflows.</p>\n<hr data-start="452" data-end="455">\n<h2 data-start="457" data-end="499">Key Features &amp; Technical Specifications</h2>\n<ul data-start="501" data-end="3288">\n<li data-start="501" data-end="625">\n<p data-start="503" data-end="625"><strong data-start="503" data-end="519">Build Volume</strong>: Approx. 255 × 255 × 260 mm — allows printing moderately large objects in one go without splitting parts.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="627" data-end="828">\n<p data-start="629" data-end="662"><strong data-start="629" data-end="659">Print Speed &amp; Acceleration</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="665" data-end="828">\n<li data-start="665" data-end="706">\n<p data-start="667" data-end="706">Maximum travel speeds up to ~600 mm/s</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="709" data-end="745">\n<p data-start="711" data-end="745">Acceleration up to ~20,000 mm/s²</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="748" data-end="828">\n<p data-start="750" data-end="828">Recommended operational speed lower (for best surface quality and reliability)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="830" data-end="1050">\n<p data-start="832" data-end="854"><strong data-start="832" data-end="851">Nozzle &amp; Hotend</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="857" data-end="1050">\n<li data-start="857" data-end="957">\n<p data-start="859" data-end="957">Standard nozzle diameter: 0.40 mm, with options for 0.60 mm or 0.80 mm to trade detail vs. speed</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="960" data-end="1050">\n<p data-start="962" data-end="1050">Maximum hotend temperature: ~300 °C, allowing use of more advanced engineering filaments</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1052" data-end="1236">\n<p data-start="1054" data-end="1072"><strong data-start="1054" data-end="1069">Build Plate</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1075" data-end="1236">\n<li data-start="1075" data-end="1128">\n<p data-start="1077" data-end="1128">Heated bed with maximum temperature up to ~110 °C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1131" data-end="1236">\n<p data-start="1133" data-end="1236">Flexible or spring-steel plate with PEI (or equivalent) surface for good adhesion and easy part release</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1238" data-end="1468">\n<p data-start="1240" data-end="1286"><strong data-start="1240" data-end="1283">Multi-colour / Multi-filament Capability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1289" data-end="1468">\n<li data-start="1289" data-end="1383">\n<p data-start="1291" data-end="1383">Enables printing with multiple filaments / colours via one or more filament-feeding modules</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1386" data-end="1468">\n<p data-start="1388" data-end="1468">Supports a setup with additional filament ports or hubs to manage several spools</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1470" data-end="1712">\n<p data-start="1472" data-end="1505"><strong data-start="1472" data-end="1502">Filament Handling &amp; Drying</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1508" data-end="1712">\n<li data-start="1508" data-end="1637">\n<p data-start="1510" data-end="1637">Built-in filament drying chamber or system maintained at moderate elevated temperature (≈ 35-55 °C) to reduce moisture issues</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1640" data-end="1712">\n<p data-start="1642" data-end="1712">Filament run-out detection and retraction or pause-on-run-out features</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1714" data-end="2006">\n<p data-start="1716" data-end="1754"><strong data-start="1716" data-end="1751">Auto-leveling &amp; Frame Stability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1757" data-end="2006">\n<li data-start="1757" data-end="1820">\n<p data-start="1759" data-end="1820">Automatic bed leveling system, reducing manual intervention</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1823" data-end="1926">\n<p data-start="1825" data-end="1926">Reinforced frame / upgraded bearings on critical axes to minimize vibration/artifact at high speeds</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1929" data-end="2006">\n<p data-start="1931" data-end="2006">Wider gantry or support in one or more axes to improve leveling consistency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2008" data-end="2221">\n<p data-start="2010" data-end="2035"><strong data-start="2010" data-end="2032">Electrical &amp; Power</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2038" data-end="2221">\n<li data-start="2038" data-end="2130">\n<p data-start="2040" data-end="2130">Single power input unit, combined printer + module draw possibly up to ~400 W under load</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2133" data-end="2221">\n<p data-start="2135" data-end="2221">Compatible with typical mains supplies; ensure stable voltage and adequate ventilation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2223" data-end="2468">\n<p data-start="2225" data-end="2259"><strong data-start="2225" data-end="2256">User Interface &amp; Monitoring</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2262" data-end="2468">\n<li data-start="2262" data-end="2368">\n<p data-start="2264" data-end="2368">Touchscreen control panel (≈ 4-5 inch capacitive display) for job setup, adjustments, firmware updates</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2371" data-end="2468">\n<p data-start="2373" data-end="2468">Integrated camera for print monitoring; potential for remote status viewing, time-lapse capture</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2470" data-end="2688">\n<p data-start="2472" data-end="2505"><strong data-start="2472" data-end="2502">Safety &amp; Recovery Features</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2508" data-end="2688">\n<li data-start="2508" data-end="2577">\n<p data-start="2510" data-end="2577">Power-loss recovery (pauses print and resumes once power resumes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2580" data-end="2641">\n<p data-start="2582" data-end="2641">Detection of filament issues (run-out, jam, entanglement)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2644" data-end="2688">\n<p data-start="2646" data-end="2688">Temperature protections for hotend / bed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2690" data-end="2899">\n<p data-start="2692" data-end="2718"><strong data-start="2692" data-end="2715">Supported Filaments</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2721" data-end="2899">\n<li data-start="2721" data-end="2779">\n<p data-start="2723" data-end="2779">Standard materials: PLA, PETG, TPU (flexible filament)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2782" data-end="2899">\n<p data-start="2784" data-end="2899">With upgrade modules: ABS, ASA, PC, PA, PP, HIPS, etc. (depending on hotend grade, enclosure or ambient conditions)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2901" data-end="3050">\n<p data-start="2903" data-end="2924"><strong data-start="2903" data-end="2921">Nozzle Options</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2927" data-end="3050">\n<li data-start="2927" data-end="2971">\n<p data-start="2929" data-end="2971">Standard fine nozzle (0.4 mm) for detail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2974" data-end="3050">\n<p data-start="2976" data-end="3050">Larger nozzles (0.6-0.8 mm) for faster printing and larger layer heights</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3052" data-end="3288">\n<p data-start="3054" data-end="3085"><strong data-start="3054" data-end="3082">Physical Characteristics</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="3088" data-end="3288">\n<li data-start="3088" data-end="3165">\n<p data-start="3090" data-end="3165">Moderate footprint; heavy components if multi-filament module(s) attached</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3168" data-end="3288">\n<p data-start="3170" data-end="3288">Packaging includes printer base, filament feeding module(s), spool hub(es), power supply, build plate, and accessories</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="3290" data-end="3293">\n<h2 data-start="3295" data-end="3339">Typical Operation Conditions &amp; Trade-Offs</h2>\n<ul data-start="3341" data-end="3962">\n<li data-start="3341" data-end="3471">\n<p data-start="3343" data-end="3471">To maintain high print quality, speed, and accuracy, regular calibration is needed (bed leveling, checking belt tensions, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3473" data-end="3634">\n<p data-start="3475" data-end="3634">Fast printing tends to introduce artifacts like ringing or ghosting, especially on tall or detailed prints; slower speeds may be used when detail is important.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3636" data-end="3769">\n<p data-start="3638" data-end="3769">Multi-filament / colour printing increases complexity: oozing, colour bleed, nozzle purging, and filament transitions require tuning.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3771" data-end="3962">\n<p data-start="3773" data-end="3962">Environmental conditions (temperature, humidity, ventilation) play a significant role, particularly when printing materials sensitive to moisture or cooling quickly (ABS, ASA, Nylon, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="256" data-end="645"><br><br></p>	<h2 data-start="243" data-end="254">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="256" data-end="645">The Anycubic Kobra 3 V2 Combo is a high-speed, multi-colour capable FDM printer with a large build volume, designed for users wanting quicker prints, colour/multi-material options, and a lot of smart features. The “Combo” refers to the fact that it includes the <strong data-start="516" data-end="527">ACE Pro</strong> module(s) that allow multi-colour/multi-filament printing (4-color, up to 8-color if two ACE Pros are used + the hub).<br></p>\n<h2 data-start="197" data-end="231">Product Description</h2>\n<p data-start="233" data-end="450">A high-performance, feature-rich FDM 3D printer designed for speed, multi-colour capability, and versatile material use. Built for serious prototyping, creative design, and flexible, high throughput printing workflows.</p>\n<hr data-start="452" data-end="455">\n<h2 data-start="457" data-end="499">Key Features &amp; Technical Specifications</h2>\n<ul data-start="501" data-end="3288">\n<li data-start="501" data-end="625">\n<p data-start="503" data-end="625"><strong data-start="503" data-end="519">Build Volume</strong>: Approx. 255 × 255 × 260 mm — allows printing moderately large objects in one go without splitting parts.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="627" data-end="828">\n<p data-start="629" data-end="662"><strong data-start="629" data-end="659">Print Speed &amp; Acceleration</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="665" data-end="828">\n<li data-start="665" data-end="706">\n<p data-start="667" data-end="706">Maximum travel speeds up to ~600 mm/s</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="709" data-end="745">\n<p data-start="711" data-end="745">Acceleration up to ~20,000 mm/s²</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="748" data-end="828">\n<p data-start="750" data-end="828">Recommended operational speed lower (for best surface quality and reliability)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="830" data-end="1050">\n<p data-start="832" data-end="854"><strong data-start="832" data-end="851">Nozzle &amp; Hotend</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="857" data-end="1050">\n<li data-start="857" data-end="957">\n<p data-start="859" data-end="957">Standard nozzle diameter: 0.40 mm, with options for 0.60 mm or 0.80 mm to trade detail vs. speed</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="960" data-end="1050">\n<p data-start="962" data-end="1050">Maximum hotend temperature: ~300 °C, allowing use of more advanced engineering filaments</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1052" data-end="1236">\n<p data-start="1054" data-end="1072"><strong data-start="1054" data-end="1069">Build Plate</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1075" data-end="1236">\n<li data-start="1075" data-end="1128">\n<p data-start="1077" data-end="1128">Heated bed with maximum temperature up to ~110 °C</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1131" data-end="1236">\n<p data-start="1133" data-end="1236">Flexible or spring-steel plate with PEI (or equivalent) surface for good adhesion and easy part release</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1238" data-end="1468">\n<p data-start="1240" data-end="1286"><strong data-start="1240" data-end="1283">Multi-colour / Multi-filament Capability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1289" data-end="1468">\n<li data-start="1289" data-end="1383">\n<p data-start="1291" data-end="1383">Enables printing with multiple filaments / colours via one or more filament-feeding modules</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1386" data-end="1468">\n<p data-start="1388" data-end="1468">Supports a setup with additional filament ports or hubs to manage several spools</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1470" data-end="1712">\n<p data-start="1472" data-end="1505"><strong data-start="1472" data-end="1502">Filament Handling &amp; Drying</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1508" data-end="1712">\n<li data-start="1508" data-end="1637">\n<p data-start="1510" data-end="1637">Built-in filament drying chamber or system maintained at moderate elevated temperature (≈ 35-55 °C) to reduce moisture issues</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1640" data-end="1712">\n<p data-start="1642" data-end="1712">Filament run-out detection and retraction or pause-on-run-out features</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1714" data-end="2006">\n<p data-start="1716" data-end="1754"><strong data-start="1716" data-end="1751">Auto-leveling &amp; Frame Stability</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="1757" data-end="2006">\n<li data-start="1757" data-end="1820">\n<p data-start="1759" data-end="1820">Automatic bed leveling system, reducing manual intervention</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1823" data-end="1926">\n<p data-start="1825" data-end="1926">Reinforced frame / upgraded bearings on critical axes to minimize vibration/artifact at high speeds</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1929" data-end="2006">\n<p data-start="1931" data-end="2006">Wider gantry or support in one or more axes to improve leveling consistency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2008" data-end="2221">\n<p data-start="2010" data-end="2035"><strong data-start="2010" data-end="2032">Electrical &amp; Power</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2038" data-end="2221">\n<li data-start="2038" data-end="2130">\n<p data-start="2040" data-end="2130">Single power input unit, combined printer + module draw possibly up to ~400 W under load</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2133" data-end="2221">\n<p data-start="2135" data-end="2221">Compatible with typical mains supplies; ensure stable voltage and adequate ventilation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2223" data-end="2468">\n<p data-start="2225" data-end="2259"><strong data-start="2225" data-end="2256">User Interface &amp; Monitoring</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2262" data-end="2468">\n<li data-start="2262" data-end="2368">\n<p data-start="2264" data-end="2368">Touchscreen control panel (≈ 4-5 inch capacitive display) for job setup, adjustments, firmware updates</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2371" data-end="2468">\n<p data-start="2373" data-end="2468">Integrated camera for print monitoring; potential for remote status viewing, time-lapse capture</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2470" data-end="2688">\n<p data-start="2472" data-end="2505"><strong data-start="2472" data-end="2502">Safety &amp; Recovery Features</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2508" data-end="2688">\n<li data-start="2508" data-end="2577">\n<p data-start="2510" data-end="2577">Power-loss recovery (pauses print and resumes once power resumes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2580" data-end="2641">\n<p data-start="2582" data-end="2641">Detection of filament issues (run-out, jam, entanglement)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2644" data-end="2688">\n<p data-start="2646" data-end="2688">Temperature protections for hotend / bed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2690" data-end="2899">\n<p data-start="2692" data-end="2718"><strong data-start="2692" data-end="2715">Supported Filaments</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2721" data-end="2899">\n<li data-start="2721" data-end="2779">\n<p data-start="2723" data-end="2779">Standard materials: PLA, PETG, TPU (flexible filament)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2782" data-end="2899">\n<p data-start="2784" data-end="2899">With upgrade modules: ABS, ASA, PC, PA, PP, HIPS, etc. (depending on hotend grade, enclosure or ambient conditions)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2901" data-end="3050">\n<p data-start="2903" data-end="2924"><strong data-start="2903" data-end="2921">Nozzle Options</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="2927" data-end="3050">\n<li data-start="2927" data-end="2971">\n<p data-start="2929" data-end="2971">Standard fine nozzle (0.4 mm) for detail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2974" data-end="3050">\n<p data-start="2976" data-end="3050">Larger nozzles (0.6-0.8 mm) for faster printing and larger layer heights</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3052" data-end="3288">\n<p data-start="3054" data-end="3085"><strong data-start="3054" data-end="3082">Physical Characteristics</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start="3088" data-end="3288">\n<li data-start="3088" data-end="3165">\n<p data-start="3090" data-end="3165">Moderate footprint; heavy components if multi-filament module(s) attached</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3168" data-end="3288">\n<p data-start="3170" data-end="3288">Packaging includes printer base, filament feeding module(s), spool hub(es), power supply, build plate, and accessories</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="3290" data-end="3293">\n<h2 data-start="3295" data-end="3339">Typical Operation Conditions &amp; Trade-Offs</h2>\n<ul data-start="3341" data-end="3962">\n<li data-start="3341" data-end="3471">\n<p data-start="3343" data-end="3471">To maintain high print quality, speed, and accuracy, regular calibration is needed (bed leveling, checking belt tensions, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3473" data-end="3634">\n<p data-start="3475" data-end="3634">Fast printing tends to introduce artifacts like ringing or ghosting, especially on tall or detailed prints; slower speeds may be used when detail is important.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3636" data-end="3769">\n<p data-start="3638" data-end="3769">Multi-filament / colour printing increases complexity: oozing, colour bleed, nozzle purging, and filament transitions require tuning.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="3771" data-end="3962">\n<p data-start="3773" data-end="3962">Environmental conditions (temperature, humidity, ventilation) play a significant role, particularly when printing materials sensitive to moisture or cooling quickly (ABS, ASA, Nylon, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="256" data-end="645"><br><br></p>	42999.00	42999.00	42999.00	0	t	f	f	t	0.00	3	t	[]	[]	[{"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443934048-676397559.png", "isPrimary": false, "sortOrder": 0}, {"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933901-61875117.jpg", "isPrimary": false, "sortOrder": 0}, {"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933887-134314735.jpg", "isPrimary": false, "sortOrder": 0}, {"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import/1784443933954-347014363.jpg", "isPrimary": false, "sortOrder": 0}, {"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/ajr3dgalaxy.firebasestorage.app/product-import