9">\n<p data-start="1469" data-end="1549">Compatible with multiple filament types: <strong data-start="1510" data-end="1537">PLA, PETG, ABS, ASA, PC</strong>, and more</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1551" data-end="1554">\n<h3 data-start="1556" data-end="1577"><strong data-start="1560" data-end="1577">Compatibility</strong></h3>\n<p data-start="1578" data-end="1647">The AMS system is compatible with the following Bambu Lab printers:</p>\n<ul data-start="1648" data-end="1800">\n<li data-start="1648" data-end="1691">\n<p data-start="1650" data-end="1691"><strong data-start="1650" data-end="1689">Bambu Lab X1 Series (X1, X1 Carbon)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1692" data-end="1734">\n<p data-start="1694" data-end="1734"><strong data-start="1694" data-end="1732">Bambu Lab P1 Series (P1, P1S, P1P)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1735" data-end="1800">\n<p data-start="1737" data-end="1800"><strong data-start="1737" data-end="1760">Bambu Lab A1 Series</strong> (when used with the AMS Lite version)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1802" data-end="1805">\n<h3 data-start="1807" data-end="1829"><strong data-start="1811" data-end="1829">Specifications</strong></h3>\n<ul data-start="1830" data-end="2099">\n<li data-start="1830" data-end="1874">\n<p data-start="1832" data-end="1874"><strong data-start="1832" data-end="1854">Filament Capacity:</strong> 4 spools per unit</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1875" data-end="1909">\n<p data-start="1877" data-end="1909"><strong data-start="1877" data-end="1899">Filament Diameter:</strong> 1.75 mm</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1910" data-end="1957">\n<p data-start="1912" data-end="1957"><strong data-start="1912" data-end="1933">Humidity Control:</strong> Active sealed chamber</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1958" data-end="2022">\n<p data-start="1960" data-end="2022"><strong data-start="1960" data-end="1985">Connection Interface:</strong> CAN bus communication with printer</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2023" data-end="2069">\n<p data